[
  {
    "slot_number": "slot-5-2-dyn-6",
    "slot_key": "Downstream export format validation",
    "slot_value": "For downstream handoff, only outputs that pass the expected format checks should be exported; anything else should be clearly flagged as unusable or provisional so another tool does not ingest it by mistake. For anything that will be handed off to another tool or used as an official downstream input, passing the checks is a firm requirement; if it does not pass, it should not be treated as a normal deliverable. The simulator should still keep a provisional record for inspection or debugging, clearly separated from the accepted output and visibly marked as not safe for downstream use. If the same intermediate product can be reused without changing the science meaning, it should be cached and the rest batched around it; if inputs differ in ways that affect the error model, processing stage, or downstream interpretation, regenerate instead of reusing. When storage or export is the bottleneck, splitting into smaller batches is usually the safest move because it allows checkpointing and avoids one huge failure. Full regeneration should be used only when the change invalidates most earlier work or when the cached material would be more expensive to manage than recreate.",
