    "slot_value": "Configuration artefacts should be versioned clearly so it is obvious which scientific model or error model they belong to; the simulator should keep track of the exact configuration used for a run, including parameter files and the random seed; users should be able to select a saved configuration rather than rebuilding it manually; adjusted scenarios should record explicit differences so runs remain auditable and rerunnable/reproducible. Results should also be traceable back to the configuration that produced them, and the run should be reproducible later or adaptable cleanly for a new scenario. When reusing a saved configuration, the latest approved version that matches the intended processing stage and science use case should be selected; if multiple variants exist, the one tied to the same validation baseline or campaign context should take precedence over a newer but unvetted option. If the saved configuration differs from the current scenario in a way that affects output meaning, it should not be silently reused; it must be explicitly adapted or treated as a new configuration. Minor operational differences may be overridden if they do not change interpretation, but any scientific difference must be surfaced and checked. Updated scientific models should be treated as versioned inputs so outputs stay tied to a known model set; new behavior should be introduced only in a controlled release with traceability in the output to identify which model version generated it. If a newer model would break compatibility with existing downstream Gaia processing, the older path should be preserved or a switch provided until the wider environment catches up. Model evolution should be explicit and managed, not automatic or surprising. The produced result must also be traceable back to the exact input configuration and the simulator version that created it, with durable references to the full run settings, model versions used, and relevant environment or transformation identifiers; if that chain cannot be reconstructed, the output is not fully auditable for comparison or reproduction.",
